{{!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Writing — the newest posts on chanmeng.org/blog, then a curated subset.
     _writingLatest is automatic: the newest meta.x_brand.latestArticleCount
     posts (default 3) not already featured, from the publications entries
     plus blog/capture/latest.json, so a post published on the site appears
     here on the next CI build with no hand edit.
     The curated rows are driven by meta.x_brand.featuredArticleIds (blog slugs; a typo fails the
     build in scripts/build.mjs, same policy as spotlightProjectIds).
     The full catalogue reaches LLM consumers via _writingAll in llms.txt /
     llms-full.txt, so trimming this list never hides an article from them.
     No badge images here by design — the section is text + links only.
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

## Writing

<sub>Field reports written while building the thing they describe — what the decision was, what broke, and what I'd do again. Everything below is self-hosted; nothing is behind a platform login.</sub>

<table>
  <colgroup>
    <col style="width:110px">
    <col>
  </colgroup>
{{#if _writingLatest.length}}  <tr><td colspan="2"><sub><b>LATEST</b></sub></td></tr>
{{#each _writingLatest}}  <tr>
    <td valign="top"><sub>{{formatDate releaseDate}}</sub></td>
    <td><strong><a href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a></strong>{{#if summary}}<br><sub>{{firstSentences (flatten summary) 1}}</sub>{{/if}}</td>
  </tr>
{{/each}}  <tr><td colspan="2"><sub><b>SELECTED</b></sub></td></tr>
{{/if}}{{#each _writingFeatured}}  <tr>
    <td valign="top"><sub>{{formatDate releaseDate}}</sub></td>
    <td><strong><a href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a></strong>{{#if summary}}<br><sub>{{firstSentences (flatten summary) 1}}</sub>{{/if}}</td>
  </tr>
{{/each}}</table>

<p><a href="{{_writingIndexUrl}}">Read all {{_writingAll.length}} articles →</a></p>
